LOCAL INNER CLASS

Interview Questions

1. What is a Local Inner Class?
-->A Local Inner Class is a class declared inside a method, constructor, or block.

      It can only be used within that method.
      
      class Test {
          void display() {
              class Local {
                  void show() {
                      System.out.println("Hello");
                  }
              }
      
              Local obj = new Local();
              obj.show();
          }
      }





2. Can we declare static methods inside a Local Inner Class?
-->No.
    A Local Inner Class cannot have static methods or static variables, except static final constants.
    
    class Local {
        static final int A = 10;   // Allowed
    }





3. Why can a Local Inner Class only access effectively final variables?
-->Because local variables are stored on the stack and disappear after the method finishes.

    Java copies the value into the Local Inner Class, so the variable must not change (must be final or effectively final).
    
    void test() {
        int x = 10;      // effectively final
    
        class Local {
            void show() {
                System.out.println(x);
            }
        }
    }






4. Where can you use Local Inner Classes?
-->You can declare them inside:
        Methods
        Constructors
        Initialization blocks

They are commonly used for:
        Event handling
        Validation
        Helper classes used only inside one method





5. Can a Local Inner Class be marked public or private?
-->No.
        A Local Inner Class cannot use access modifiers like:
        
        public
        private
        protected
        static
        
        It is visible only inside the method where it is declared.




6. How do you access a Local Inner Class outside the method?
-->You cannot.

A Local Inner Class exists only inside the method where it is declared.

void display() {
    class Local {
    }

    Local obj = new Local();   // Allowed
}

// Outside display(), Local cannot be accessed.







7. Give a real-time use case of a Local Inner Class (Security, event handling).
-->Example: Event Handling

class Button {
    void click() {

        class ClickHandler {
            void handle() {
                System.out.println("Button Clicked");
            }
        }

        ClickHandler obj = new ClickHandler();
        obj.handle();
    }
}

Other real-time uses:
        Security checks
        Form validation
        Event handling
        Temporary helper classes
        Database query processing within a method


